<% content_for :title, "Reviewer preview — Sutura" %>

<div class="mb-6 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 rounded-2xl border border-amber-200/25 bg-amber-200/10 p-5">
  <div><p class="text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-amber-300">Guided tour · step 2 of 3</p><p class="mt-2 text-sm text-stone-200">This is the public, read-only version of the decision screen. Nothing you click here changes scholarly data.</p></div>
  <%= link_to "Back to the reader", text_line_path(@scroll.slug, @source.column.position, @source.anchor.split("-line-").last), class: "text-xs text-amber-200 hover:text-amber-100" %>
</div>

<header class="mb-8 max-w-4xl">
  <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-stone-500">Candidate review · <%= @scroll.identifier %> · <%= @source.metadata["citation"] || @source.label %></p>
  <h1 class="mt-3 font-serif text-4xl md:text-5xl">Would you connect these passages?</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-400">Sutura proposes a lead; the reviewer decides whether the resemblance is philologically meaningful. The algorithm never promotes its own result to an accepted claim.</p>
</header>

<div class="grid gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2">
  <article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-stone-900/60 p-6">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between"><p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-amber-300">Recovered passage</p><span class="rounded-full bg-emerald-400/10 px-3 py-1 text-[10px] uppercase text-emerald-300"><%= @source.reading.editorial_status %></span></div>
    <p class="mt-7 font-serif text-2xl leading-relaxed text-stone-100"><%= @source.reading.diplomatic_text %></p>
    <p class="mt-6 border-t border-white/10 pt-5 text-sm leading-6 text-stone-400"><%= @source.reading.translation %></p>
    <p class="mt-5 text-[11px] text-stone-600"><%= @source.metadata["citation"] %> · source transcription preserved verbatim</p>
  </article>

  <article class="rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-stone-900/60 p-6">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between"><p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-sky-300">Comparison passage</p><span class="rounded-full bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 text-[10px] uppercase text-stone-400">unreviewed</span></div>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xs text-sky-300"><%= @target.corpus_work.author %> · <%= @target.corpus_work.title %> · <%= @target.citation %></p>
    <p class="mt-4 font-serif text-2xl leading-relaxed text-stone-100"><%= @target.content %></p>
    <p class="mt-6 border-t border-white/10 pt-5 text-[11px] text-stone-600">Curated comparison corpus · <%= @target.corpus_work.metadata["license"] %></p>
  </article>
</div>

<section class="mt-5 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-stone-900/40 p-6">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-3"><div><p class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-stone-500">Why the system proposed it</p><h2 class="mt-2 font-serif text-2xl">Evidence by independent channel</h2></div><p class="text-xs text-stone-500">RRF score <%= number_with_precision(@match.combined_score, precision: 5) %></p></div>
  <div class="mt-6 grid gap-3 md:grid-cols-2">
    <% @match.match_evidences.each do |evidence| %>
      <article class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-black/20 p-4">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between"><span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-stone-300"><%= evidence.channel %></span><span class="font-mono text-xs text-amber-200"><%= number_with_precision(evidence.score, precision: 3) %></span></div>
        <dl class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-xs">
          <% evidence.details.each do |key, value| %><div><dt class="text-stone-600"><%= key.humanize %></dt><dd class="mt-1 leading-5 text-stone-300"><%= Array(value).join(", ") %></dd></div><% end %>
        </dl>
      </article>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-5 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-stone-900/60 p-6">
  <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] lg:items-end">
    <div><label class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-stone-500" for="review-note">Reviewer note</label><textarea id="review-note" disabled class="mt-3 min-h-24 w-full resize-none rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-black/20 p-4 text-sm text-stone-500" placeholder="In the authenticated workspace, the reviewer records philological reasoning here."></textarea></div>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2"><button disabled class="cursor-not-allowed rounded-full bg-emerald-300/20 px-5 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-200 opacity-70">Accept link</button><button disabled class="cursor-not-allowed rounded-full bg-amber-300/15 px-5 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-amber-200 opacity-70">Needs work</button><button disabled class="cursor-not-allowed rounded-full bg-rose-300/15 px-5 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-rose-200 opacity-70">Reject</button></div>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-5 text-stone-600">Authenticated decisions are append-only, attributed to a reviewer and included in the audit trail. Rejection requires a note.</p>
</section>

<aside class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-5 rounded-2xl border border-emerald-300/15 bg-emerald-300/5 p-6">
  <div><p class="text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-emerald-300">Step 3 · citable output</p><p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-stone-300">Once accepted, the connection can enter EpiDoc, JSON-LD and CSV exports. Pending and rejected leads never become confirmed assertions.</p></div>
  <div class="flex gap-2"><%= link_to "JSON-LD", graph_export_path(@scroll.slug), class: "rounded-full border border-white/15 px-4 py-2 text-xs hover:border-emerald-200/40" %><%= link_to "CSV", matches_export_path(@scroll.slug), class: "rounded-full border border-white/15 px-4 py-2 text-xs hover:border-emerald-200/40" %></div>
</aside>
